        <detaileddescription>
<para>Maximum number of documents fetched per negative term when scanning the secondary index. 0 means no limit. Default 100&apos;000.</para>
<para>For common terms this bound prevents unbounded memory use, but it may result in <emphasis>incomplete</emphasis> exclusion when a negative term matches more documents than <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_negative_keyword_filter_1_1_config_1ac1e690ef20cb80952bc75be7dfbcfe5c" kindref="member">max_exclude_scan</ref></computeroutput>. Set to 0 to disable the limit and guarantee complete exclusion at the cost of higher memory. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
